            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0165" n="45" xml:id="pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A4a/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Siam</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Brodie</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-02T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7. You may informally advise the Minister for Foreign Affairs that the Secretary
                    of State is gratified to learn the sentiments expressed in first paragraph of
                    your number I January 7, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>You should explain to the Minister for Foreign Affairs that the Four-Power Pact
                    relates only to those problems which concern insular possessions and insular
                    dominions in the region of the Pacific.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
